{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00154",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.02,
      "end_seconds": 3.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Right, come in and get settled."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.6,
      "end_seconds": 8.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Thanks, um, doctor. It's been a long few days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.37,
      "end_seconds": 14.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.09,
      "end_seconds": 17.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Lovely day outside, isn't it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 19.0,
      "end_seconds": 22.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "It is, I almost forgot I was coming here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.28,
      "end_seconds": 29.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "What seems to be the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.28,
      "end_seconds": 36.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "I'm here because of more breathlessness than usual. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.65,
      "end_seconds": 39.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.15,
      "end_seconds": 43.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.98,
      "text": "It's, It's been like this since Friday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.25,
      "end_seconds": 47.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.51,
      "end_seconds": 50.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.16,
      "end_seconds": 53.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.14,
      "end_seconds": 61.6,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "A wheeze goes along with it, most of the time. The wheeze? That's been for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 63.08,
      "end_seconds": 66.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "What about a rattling chest, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.61,
      "end_seconds": 70.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Yes, actually. About rattling chest, I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.35,
      "end_seconds": 75.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Any weight loss, confusion or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.28,
      "end_seconds": 79.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "No, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.85,
      "end_seconds": 84.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "What about swollen ankles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.34,
      "end_seconds": 87.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "No, no swollen ankles."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.62,
      "end_seconds": 90.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.64,
      "end_seconds": 93.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.32,
      "end_seconds": 96.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.0,
      "end_seconds": 99.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.02,
      "end_seconds": 102.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Are you on any tablets or medication?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.57,
      "end_seconds": 112.0,
      "duration_seconds": 8.43,
      "text": "I take Tiotropium inhaler, once a day for my chest. I take telmisartan, 40 milligrams, once a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 113.41,
      "end_seconds": 120.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.5,
      "text": "Doctor, you know, I think the last prescription for the telmisartan was 20 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.6,
      "end_seconds": 125.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Right. Do you happen to have the current prescription here?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.45,
      "end_seconds": 134.55,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Omeprazole. I take it 20 milligrams, once a day for the reflux."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.96,
      "end_seconds": 141.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.82,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all? Bear with me, I'm just building up the picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.16,
      "end_seconds": 148.65,
      "duration_seconds": 6.49,
      "text": "Shellfish. I come out in... well, vomiting. Yes, latex, it gives me a rash on my hands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.37,
      "end_seconds": 162.65,
      "duration_seconds": 13.28,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.27,
      "end_seconds": 165.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.68,
      "end_seconds": 168.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.3,
      "end_seconds": 172.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "Uh, no, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.21,
      "end_seconds": 187.33,
      "duration_seconds": 14.12,
      "text": "It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.67,
      "end_seconds": 190.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.47,
      "end_seconds": 193.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.54,
      "end_seconds": 210.24,
      "duration_seconds": 15.7,
      "text": "I've got COPD. I have high blood pressure, for about ten years. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. Well, I've got acid reflux. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.29,
      "end_seconds": 218.98,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "I see. Yes, I can see the COPD in your file as well. Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.58,
      "end_seconds": 231.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "For the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 232.89,
      "end_seconds": 240.59,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Respiratory rate 22, saturation 93 percent. Temperature 36.9, pulse 97, pressure 141 over 85."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.11,
      "end_seconds": 244.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.47,
      "end_seconds": 249.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 249.83,
      "end_seconds": 250.7,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.24,
      "end_seconds": 253.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.6,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 266.1,
      "end_seconds": 271.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.07,
      "text": "Air entry is reduced on both sides with a prolonged breathing out phase."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.89,
      "end_seconds": 275.2,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.28,
      "end_seconds": 291.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.42,
      "text": "There's some wheeze, and no swelling in the legs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.93,
      "end_seconds": 324.99,
      "duration_seconds": 28.06,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like a flare-up of COPD. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. It could also be heart failure, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.52,
      "end_seconds": 328.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.96,
      "end_seconds": 342.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.67,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with a flare-up of COPD do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had more breathlessness than usual, since Friday, moderate, and no chest pain or confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 343.02,
      "end_seconds": 345.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Yes, um, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 345.9,
      "end_seconds": 356.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.89,
      "text": "Let's get blood tests, for infective exacerbation. I'd like to arrange a chest X-ray for breathlessness. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.93,
      "end_seconds": 358.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.02,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.28,
      "end_seconds": 380.02,
      "duration_seconds": 20.74,
      "text": "I'm prescribing doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day, for five days. That's for chest infection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. I'd like you to take prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day, for five days. It's for COPD flare-up. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.35,
      "end_seconds": 390.68,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 393.54,
      "end_seconds": 394.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 395.94,
      "end_seconds": 407.08,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if you become more breathless or your lips turn blue, call us the same day or go to emergency. I'd like to see you again in one week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.78,
      "end_seconds": 411.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.67,
      "text": "Okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.38,
      "end_seconds": 416.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Just to confirm, what are the next steps as you understand them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.88,
      "end_seconds": 428.45,
      "duration_seconds": 10.57,
      "text": "So, you know, I take the doxycycline, 100 milligrams, twice a day and take the prednisolone, 30 milligrams, once a day. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 429.68,
      "end_seconds": 434.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.33,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.16,
      "end_seconds": 437.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.88,
      "end_seconds": 439.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}